# Files specified here are not required for Docker
# Excluding them helps keep the build context lite
node_modules
docs
tests
dist
.git
.github

# Application runtime state.
#
# These directories are the bind-mount targets the stack fills at run time, and
# their contents belong to the *containers'* own uids — which the process sending
# the build context is not. A run leaves them behind, so without these lines the
# next build fails with
#
#   ERROR: error from sender: open .../OnlyOffice/db: permission denied
#
# for every user who is not root, and even when it succeeds (root can read them)
# every build uploads the whole database, cache and log tree to the builder.
# Neither is acceptable: none of this is an input to this image.
Zulip/data
Zulip/database
Zulip/rabbitmq
Zulip/redis
Filebrowser/data
Filebrowser/office-cache
OnlyOffice/data
OnlyOffice/db
OnlyOffice/lib
OnlyOffice/logs
Mailcow/data
Traefik/certs
Traefik/logs
Traefik/acme.json

# Generated secrets and harness state, for the same reason: written per run, never
# an input to this image. `user-data/conf.yml`, which the image *does* carry, is
# deliberately not listed here.
Zulip/secrets
user-data/e2e
user-data/broker
user-data/config-backups

# The only things needed to build the Dockerfile are:
# Depens: package.json, yarn.lock
# Setup:  tsconfig.json, vite.config.mjs
# Client: index.html, src/, public/
# Server: services/, server.js
# Config: user-data/conf.yml
